   "id": "ketubot.82b.7",
   "daf": "82b",
   "sentenceId": 6,
   "he": "גֵּרְשָׁהּ — אֵין לָהּ אֶלָּא כְּתוּבָּתָהּ. גֵּרְשָׁהּ — אִין, לֹא גֵּרְשָׁהּ — לָא. קָא מַשְׁמַע לַן כִּדְרַבִּי אַבָּא.",
   "en": "§ The mishna states that if «he divorced her she has only her marriage contract.» There is no lien upon the property, and he may therefore sell it. The Gemara infers: If «he divorced her, yes,» that is the case, but if «he did not divorce her, no,» it is not. The tanna here «teaches us» indirectly that the halakha is «in accordance with Rabbi Abba,» who claims that the only way he can gain full control of all the property is by divorcing her."
  }
 ],
